From f83cd4f83cd52b6542df6e1d951523aac091c9b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adesh chaudhari <superbhel7@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 08:28:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] feat(frontend): wire the catalogue pages and delete
 mockData.js
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

YG-5, YG-7, YG-13, YG-14. Every rename in plan section 4 applied.

mockData.js is gone entirely — no page imports it any more. The hero carousel
now features real events, so an empty database shows an empty state instead of
three events that do not exist.

Fields with no backing column are dropped rather than faked (plan 6): rating,
reviewsCount, organizer, venueAddress, terms, tag/tagColor, originalPrice, and
the per-tier features list. An event has no price at all — price lives on
ticket tiers, which are per show — so cards link to the show picker instead of
quoting a number.

Removed the client-side convenience fee and 18% GST. The backend computes
totalAmount as the sum of unitPrice x quantity and nothing else, so those lines
showed the user a total the server never agrees with (plan 2.5).

Quantity selectors cap at availableQty and disable at zero; the server still
rejects overselling atomically with a 400 we surface verbatim.
